  "notes": [
    "No hysteresis. A slow or noisy edge makes the output chatter through the transition, sometimes several times. If the input comes from an RC, a long cable, a sensor or a switch, use the 74HC14 instead.",
    "Same pin arrangement as the 74HC14, so the two are interchangeable in a socket. The 14 is a strict upgrade for about the same money.",
    "Tie unused inputs to a rail. Six floating inverter inputs will happily oscillate and heat the chip.",
    "Two inverters and an RC make a ring oscillator, but without hysteresis it is jittery. Again, the 74HC14 does this properly."
  ],
